\ ==============================================================================
\ errors.irundykue
\ Irundykue-syry : THROW codes and messages (scope v1)
\ ==============================================================================
\
\ This file is the counterpart of errno.h for the dialect: it gives a name to
\ every THROW code that the system generates. Forth 2012 defines the numbers
\ (Table 9.1) but no such file, so the names below are the project's own.
\
\ Source of truth
\   src/Irundykue/Exception/Taxonomy.idr fixes the codes, and the Idris compiler
\   checks that they are distinct and lie in the right ranges. docs/EXCEPTIONS.md
\   describes the scope. Every constant below names its Idris constructor in the
\   comment after it, and "make errors-check" compares the two.
\
\ Rules (Forth 2012, sections 9.3.1 and 9.3.4)
\   -255 ... -1       used only as assigned by the standard
\   -4095 ... -256    used only as assigned by a system
\   Programs must not define THROW values in -4095 ... -1.
\   A condition of Table 9.1 keeps its standard number, whether it is thrown or
\   absorbed by CO-EXECUTE. The residue that CO-EXECUTE hands to a recovery
\   operator is the THROW code, not the raw ESR_EL1 value.
\
\ Not generated in this version
\   Every other code of Table 9.1, for example stack overflow and underflow,
\   undefined word and control structure mismatch. The behaviour of the system for
\   these conditions is not specified in this version; see docs/EXCEPTIONS.md.
\
\ Status
\   The numbers and the names are final for scope v1. The interpreter does not
\   load this file yet.

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ 1. Standard codes (the numbers of Forth 2012, Table 9.1)
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  -1 CONSTANT ERR-ABORT            \ AbortExplicit      ABORT
  -2 CONSTANT ERR-ABORT-MESSAGE    \ AbortWithMessage   ABORT"
  -8 CONSTANT ERR-DICT-OVERFLOW    \ DictionaryOverflow dictionary overflow
 -20 CONSTANT ERR-READ-ONLY        \ ReadOnlyFault      write to a read-only location
 -23 CONSTANT ERR-ALIGNMENT        \ AlignmentFault     address alignment exception

\ Singularities. CO-EXECUTE absorbs these three; outside CO-EXECUTE the same
\ number is thrown.
  -9 CONSTANT ERR-INVALID-ADDRESS  \ TranslationAbort   invalid memory address
 -10 CONSTANT ERR-DIV-BY-ZERO      \ DivByZeroResidue   division by zero
 -11 CONSTANT ERR-RESULT-RANGE     \ ContractionDefect  result out of range (checked arithmetic only)

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ 2. System codes (the dialect; -4095 ... -256)
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-256 CONSTANT ERR-TME-ABORT        \ TmeConflict        hardware transaction aborted
-257 CONSTANT ERR-PAC-FAILURE      \ PacViolation       pointer authentication failed
-258 CONSTANT ERR-ORTHO-SIZE       \ Sve2DimensionError orthogonal stack transfer is not exactly four cells

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ 3. Classification
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ n is in the range that Forth 2012 assigns to the standard (-255 ... -1).
: ERR-STANDARD? ( n -- flag )
  -255 0 WITHIN
;

\ n is in the range that Forth 2012 leaves to the system (-4095 ... -256).
: ERR-SYSTEM? ( n -- flag )
  -4095 -255 WITHIN
;

\ n is a singularity: a code that CO-EXECUTE can absorb.
: ERR-SINGULARITY? ( n -- flag )
  DUP ERR-DIV-BY-ZERO = OVER ERR-INVALID-ADDRESS = OR
  SWAP ERR-RESULT-RANGE = OR
;

\ n is a code that this version generates.
: ERR-KNOWN? ( n -- flag )
  CASE
    ERR-ABORT           OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-ABORT-MESSAGE   OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-DICT-OVERFLOW   OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-INVALID-ADDRESS OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-DIV-BY-ZERO     OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-RESULT-RANGE    OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-READ-ONLY       OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-ALIGNMENT       OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-TME-ABORT       OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-PAC-FAILURE     OF TRUE ENDOF
    ERR-ORTHO-SIZE      OF TRUE ENDOF
    FALSE SWAP
  ENDCASE
;

\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
\ 4. Messages
\ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ The text of a code. The wording of Table 9.1 is used for the standard codes,
\ except -2, which is spelled out because the string cannot hold a quote.
: ERR-MESSAGE ( n -- c-addr u )
  CASE
    ERR-ABORT           OF S" ABORT"                                   ENDOF
    ERR-ABORT-MESSAGE   OF S" ABORT with a message"                    ENDOF
    ERR-DICT-OVERFLOW   OF S" dictionary overflow"                     ENDOF
    ERR-INVALID-ADDRESS OF S" invalid memory address"                  ENDOF
    ERR-DIV-BY-ZERO     OF S" division by zero"                        ENDOF
    ERR-RESULT-RANGE    OF S" result out of range"                     ENDOF
    ERR-READ-ONLY       OF S" write to a read-only location"           ENDOF
    ERR-ALIGNMENT       OF S" address alignment exception"             ENDOF
    ERR-TME-ABORT       OF S" hardware transaction aborted"            ENDOF
    ERR-PAC-FAILURE     OF S" pointer authentication failed"           ENDOF
    ERR-ORTHO-SIZE      OF S" orthogonal stack transfer is not exactly four cells" ENDOF
    S" unknown error" ROT
  ENDCASE
;
